  "report_period": "Week 16 (10th Apr to 17th Apr 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Drydel Shipping have committed their Ultramax \"Amore\" 61/2012 Shin Kasado, Japan (SS/DD 11/2027) to Chinese interests at USD 20,4 mill. Remind you that three months ago, the \"Explorer Africa\" 61/2012 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 04/2027) was sold at USD 19,2 mill. The Supramax \"Sunny Royal\" 58/2011 Kawasaki, Japan (SS 11/2030, DD 12/2028) of Kawasaki Kisen Kaisha was committed at USD 18,4 mill. For reference, the one-year-younger \"Eleen Eva\" 58/2012 Shin Kurushima, Japan (SS 10/2030, DD 12/2028) was sold back in December at low USD 17 mill. Moreover, the \"Honour\" 57/2010 Cosco, China (SS 07/2030, DD 06/2028) was committed at low USD 13 mill. Note that a month ago, the \"Papa John\" 56/2010 Qingshan, China (SS 11/2030, DD 12/2028) was sold at the same price. In addition, the \"Poseidon S\" 53/2008 Iwagi, Japan (SS 03/2030, DD 03/2028) was committed to Turkish interests at USD 13 mill, while the sister vessel \"Mercury Ocean\" 53/2008 Iwagi, Japan (SS/DD 04/2026) was sold a couple of weeks ago basis SS/DD passed at USD 13 mill also. On the Handysize sector, Astrobulk committed the \"Astro Orion\" 37/2017 Avic, China (SS/DD 05/2027) to Greek interests at USD 21 mill. For comparison, the one-year-younger \"Nord Santiago\" 39/2018 Jiangmen, China (SS 07/2028, DD 08/2026) was sold a month ago at USD 22 mill.",
    "tankers": "MOL India have committed the VLCC \"Kasagisan\" 302/2006 Mitsui, Japan (SS 08/2029, DD 08/2027) to undisclosed interests at rgn USD 59 mill basis \"As Is, Where Is\" within AG/Japan range. Note that in March, the \"Kiho\" 300/2006 IHI, Japan (SS 02/2029, DD 02/2027) was sold at USD 51,5 mill. Following the sale of the Suezmax \"Stena Sunshine\" 159/2013 Samsung, Korea (SS/DD 09/2027, Scrubber fitted) in March at USD 63 mill, Stena Bulk have now committed the one-year-older \"Stena Surprise\" 158/2012 Sungdong, Korea (SS/DD 05/2027, Scrubber fitted) to Greek interests at rgn USD 61 mill. Performance Shipping have committed their Aframax \"P. Aliki\" 105/2010 Hyundai, Korea (SS 06/2030, DD 08/2028, Scrubber fitted) to clients of Trafigura at USD 42,65 mill basis delivery Q3 2026. Remind you that the one- year-older \"P. Sophia\" 105/2009 Hyundai, Korea (SS 09/2029, DD 11/2027) was sold back in February at USD 35,65 mill. The LR1 \"PM Imperial\" 76/2007 Dalian, China (SS 08/2030, DD 08/2028) was committed at USD 20 mill, while the one-year-older \"Pan Cake\" 72/2006 Dalian, China (SS/DD freshly passed) was committed at USD 19 mill. Vroon Tankers have committed the MR1 \"East Coast\" 37/2005 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 03/2030, DD 04/2028, Scrubber fitted, Ice Class 1B) to Greek interests at USD 11,7 mill. For comparison, same owners committed in March the sister vessel \"Acadian\" 37/2005 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 07/2030, DD 07/2028, Scrubber fitted, Ice Class 1B) at USD 10 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds with redelivery in the Singapore-Japan range were reported at usd 16,000 pd, while trips with redelivery in China were fixed around usd 19,000/23,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into South East Asia were fixed at levels ranging from usd 18,500/22,000 pd. China trips via Indonesia into South China were reported around usd 16,000/19,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into the Singapore-Japan range were fixed between usd 18,000/23,000 pd. Additionally, India trips via East Coast South America into Singapore-Japan were reported at usd 20,000/22,000 pd. Continent trips via North Coast South America into Singapore-Japan were fixed at usd 25,500 pd. On the period front, Kamsarmaxes were reported fixed at usd 17,750 pd for 11/13 months employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "Indonesia trips into East Coast India ranged from usd 18,000 to usd 19,000 pd. Indonesia trips into West Coast India were fixed at usd 23,500 pd. South East Asia trips into the East Africa were reported around usd 21,000 pd.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Trips via East Kalimantan into South China were fixed around usd 16,000 pd."
    }
  },
